First, we evaluate each term inside the ceiling functions separately.

Starting with $\sqrt{\frac{9}{4}}$, we have:
\begin{align*}
\sqrt{\frac{9}{4}} &= \frac{\sqrt{9}}{\sqrt{4}} \\
&= \frac{3}{2} \\
&= 1.5
\end{align*}

Next, we evaluate $\frac{9}{4}$:
\begin{align*}
\frac{9}{4} &= 2.25
\end{align*}

Finally, we evaluate $\left(\frac{9}{4}\right)^2$:
\begin{align*}
\left(\frac{9}{4}\right)^2 &= \frac{81}{16} \\
&= 5.0625
\end{align*}

Now, we apply the ceiling function to each of these values:
\begin{align*}
\left\lceil 1.5 \right\rceil &= 2 \\
\left\lceil 2.25 \right\rceil &= 3 \\
\left\lceil 5.0625 \right\rceil &= 6
\end{align*}

Adding these results together, we get:
\begin{align*}
2 + 3 + 6 &= 11
\end{align*}

Therefore, the value of the given expression is $\boxed{11}$.
